# Kit MIDI channel owns Note On/Off. GLO partch can put 909 and 303A on one channel;
# a GM kick on that channel must not open the 303A gate (MIDI consume, no leak).
# midiheld: bit 0 = 303A gate. Defaults stay distinct (MID-02); this remaps like GLO.
wait 50
expect midiheld 0

# Remap 909 (part 0) and 303A (part 2) both onto MIDI channel 10 (0x99 / 0x89).
partch 0 10
partch 2 10

# Kick (GM 36) on the shared kit channel — 303A must stay off.
midi 99 24 64 0
wait 20
expect midiheld 0

# Non-GM pitch on the kit channel is still consumed (no bass leak).
midi 99 30 64 0
wait 20
expect midiheld 0

# Control: 303A alone on channel 2 still opens on the same pitch.
partch 2 2
midi 91 24 64 0
wait 20
expect midiheld 1
midi 81 24 00 0
wait 20
expect midiheld 0

# Defaults restored for later scenarios in a shared host process (host is one-shot).
partch 0 10
partch 2 2
